From cb7168f0be06402d939d8769be48aa2504fd209e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:45:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the menus in Dolby Vision do not take the
 output that the start signal set up for a video

The menus in Dolby Vision (CDVMenus) start while nothing holds the
output (DVMenusState(): busy). The Dolby Vision signal that is set up
with the change of mode of a video, before its first picture
(CDVStartSignal), captures the output and keeps it for that video until
its renderer takes it, the player stops or CDVStartSignal::WAIT_MS pass
(m_dvStartWaits). That wait was not among what makes the menus wait.
Where the player stopped in it, the menus could start in the next frame,
before PresentRender() saw the stop, on the output that BeginDVBridge()
finds captured; PresentRender() then draws the menus and returns before
it reaches the end of that wait, so the wait stayed until the output was
restored: the output could not be moved to another display meanwhile,
and a video that took the output over from the menus left it standing.

The menus now wait while the start signal waits, as they do for the
other waits of native output (m_dvEndDeferred, m_dvMovePending,
m_dvHandOver); the wait ends as before, with the ordinary output
restored, and the menus start after it.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index daca72a..b3b1d49 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -3896,8 +3896,10 @@ CDVMenus::State CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::DVMenusState(bool forStart)
             g_modeChangeOutput != 0;
   // (what is left of a video on the output, a change of mode held, an output that a flip that did not come
   // turned off; and the composition of the GUI over HDR, which the renderer of an HDR video has on)
+  // (and the output that the Dolby Vision signal set up for a video that has not taken it yet:
+  // CDVStartSignal)
   s.busy = CWinSystemGbm::OutputMoveBlocked() || m_dvEndDeferred || m_dvMovePending || m_dvHandOver ||
-           m_flipOutputOff || m_guiCompositing;
+           m_dvStartWaits || m_flipOutputOff || m_guiCompositing;
   s.looked = DVMenusDisplayLooked();
   s.window = m_nWidth == DVBRIDGE::TRANSPORT_WIDTH && m_nHeight == DVBRIDGE::TRANSPORT_HEIGHT &&
              GetOutputBitDepth() == 8 && m_renderableType == EGL_OPENGL_ES3_BIT;
